# Money neutrality test: does the size of the money stock change the
# *real* economy, or only the price level?
#
# At month 200 -- inside the 1000-month burn-in -- every household is handed
# 50, raising money in circulation from 100,000 to 150,000 and leaving 800
# months for the economy to re-equilibrate before measurement begins. That
# timing is the whole point: `scenarios/stimulus.scenario` fires mid-
# measurement and shows the *transient*, which is a different question.
#
# The prediction, if Lengnick v1 is a closed circular flow in which the price
# level floats until real demand equals capacity: prices and wages rise by
# roughly 50% and unemployment does not move at all. If unemployment instead
# falls and stays down, money is not neutral here and creating money is by
# itself a lever on the real economy.
#
#   python3 scripts/ensemble.py --seeds 20 --scenario scenarios/money_plus50.scenario
#
# The seed is overridden by the ensemble's --seed, so this one file is the
# treatment applied to all 20 histories.

atc-scenario 1
seed 1

200 issue_all 0 50
